# Research content must never land here (enforced by CI guardrail too)
research/
decisions/
book/
*-decisions.md

# `.specify/decisions` is a LOCAL SYMLINK to the Antreprenoriat research repo
# (research/G19-fix-fpml-iso20022/decisions/speckit), where the gate/verify
# records are tracked and backed up. It needs its own entry: the `decisions/`
# rule above ends in a slash, so it matches DIRECTORIES only, and git treats a
# symlink as a file no matter what it points at. Without this line the symlink
# shows up as `?? .specify/decisions`, which fails
# `fixpp::dict::codegen-build-graph-check` (it asserts `git status --porcelain`
# is empty) and would otherwise be committed into fixpp as a dangling absolute
# path in every CI checkout.
.specify/decisions

.claude
# Vendored spec-kit skills under .claude/ stay ignored EXCEPT the
# locally-patched files: speckit-implement/SKILL.md carries the project's
# pipeline.md step-9 checklist-audit routing + step-5a phase-implementer
# binding; speckit-analyze/SKILL.md carries the pipeline.md [I] (2026-05-22)
# spec-analyzer-agent canonical-executor binding (both have LOCAL PATCH
# headers); speckit-tasks/SKILL.md carries the mandatory close-out tasks
# (catalogue-flip + feature-completeness audit, Gate-B preconditions per
# Article XVII §8 — mirrors the tracked tasks-template.md block). Tracked so
# a spec-kit `integration upgrade` cannot silently revert them to vanilla.
# Re-include each path level, re-exclude its contents, whitelist the file.
!.claude/
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
.claude/skills/*
!.claude/skills/speckit-implement/
.claude/skills/speckit-implement/*
!.claude/skills/speckit-implement/SKILL.md
!.claude/skills/speckit-analyze/
.claude/skills/speckit-analyze/*
!.claude/skills/speckit-analyze/SKILL.md
!.claude/skills/speckit-tasks/
.claude/skills/speckit-tasks/*
!.claude/skills/speckit-tasks/SKILL.md

# libFuzzer corpus.
#
# ⚠️ THE RATIONALE THAT USED TO BE HERE -- "regenerated on each fuzz run; not source
# of truth" -- WAS TRUE WHEN WRITTEN (feature 008, 2026-05-21) AND IS NOW FALSE.
# #213 wired `tests/fuzz/corpus/<name>/` to auto-register a `fuzz_replay_<name>`
# ctest, so a committed corpus IS source of truth: it is the regression evidence
# that harness replays in CI. The six corpora tracked today survive these patterns
# only because they were added BEFORE them -- .gitignore does not apply to files
# already tracked -- so the rules read as if corpora are untracked while the
# repository says otherwise.
#
# What these patterns are still for: keeping AD-HOC local fuzz output (a scratch
# `-runs=...` corpus dir) from being committed by accident. A corpus that is meant
# to ship must therefore be negated explicitly below, which makes adding one a
# deliberate line someone wrote rather than a side effect of running the fuzzer.
tests/fuzz/corpus/*
tests/config/fuzz/corpus/*
!tests/fuzz/corpus/message_store/
!tests/fuzz/corpus/decimal_parse/
!tests/fuzz/corpus/dict_xml_loader/
!tests/fuzz/corpus/file_cert_source/
!tests/fuzz/corpus/orchestra_loader/
!tests/fuzz/corpus/session_cancellation/
!tests/fuzz/corpus/transport_read_path/
!tests/fuzz/corpus/wire_nested_slice/
# ⚠️ ONE LINE PER SHIPPED CORPUS, and tests/fuzz/CMakeLists.txt now FATALs on a
# harness with no corpus (#408) -- so a seed left ignored here does not fail
# quietly: file(GLOB) finds nothing on the runner and the empty-corpus
# FATAL_ERROR reddens the asan lane. Verify a new corpus with
# `git check-ignore -v tests/fuzz/corpus/<name>/<seed>` BEFORE pushing --
# locally the untracked-but-present dir configures fine, so this is a
# CI-only red if it is wrong.

# Python wheel build output (cibuildwheel / build-wheel.sh)
wheelhouse/

# 069-v44-all-families local byte-identity baseline (reproducible via
# `fixpp-codegen --families official`; not a source-of-truth artifact)
specs/069-v44-all-families/baseline/

# spec-kit CLI catalog cache (ephemeral, regenerated)
.specify/integrations/.cache/
